    <statement><p>Find the differential of the function
<m>f(x,y) = xe^{y}</m> at <m>(2,0)</m>.</p>
<p><m>df =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1dx+2dy</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>df = f_x \, dx + f_y \, dy</m>.
Finding the partial derivatives, we have
<m>f_x = e^{y}</m>, so <m>f_x(2,0) = 1</m>, and
<m>f_y = xe^{y}</m>, so <m>f_y(2,0) = 2</m>.
Thus, <m>df = 1dx+2dy</m>.



</solution>
